# rule.forbid.workarounds

> **never work around a failure. diagnose to root cause and fix there; when the failed tool is one you build, the failure IS the defect report.**

workaround = a change to an input, declaration, config, or your conduct that quiets a failure while its cause stands.

bar, a pit of success: correct use meets no friction; any friction is a critical defect, fixed now. wrong state unreachable, or caught once at the cheapest moment with the exact fix printed · soundness by construction, not a list a human syncs · the cure ships with a clamp (red without, green with).

test: **"did the cause of this failure change, or only my input to it?"** input only → workaround; fix the cause.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you edit a declaration/glob/config so a refusal stops | why did the tool let that state exist? |
| one cause refuses many times | check sits at the wrong moment; move it |
| contract sound only while a human syncs a list | the contract is the defect |
| you must read a doc to use your own tool right | friction is the defect |
| you write "the tool did its job" about a failure you hit | sharpest cue |
| same failure kind twice | the first fix was a workaround |

blocker: input/declaration/config patched while the cause stands · a workaround recorded instead of a fix · dogfooder friction left unfixed in its round · repeated refusal from one cause left in place · a contract that needs hand upkeep.
